Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: no geometry shaders on Turnip, as on Android

Geometry shaders are very expensive on tilers, so the Android build never uses them. On Linux,
Mesa Turnip (Adreno) exposes geometryShader but not VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric, so
CalcExtraConfig() added a geometry shader to every pipeline with per-fragment lighting. Treat
Turnip like Android: the disk cache already handles a device without geometry shaders.

---
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_instance.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_instance.h
@@ -122,7 +122,9 @@
         // cost even if it hurts accuracy somewhat. TODO: Make this an option
         return false;
 #else
-        return features.geometryShader;
+        // Asgard: Turnip (Adreno) is a tiler too, and has no fragment shader barycentrics, so every lit draw got a
+        // geometry shader on Linux. Same trade as Android: slightly less exact lighting interpolation.
+        return features.geometryShader && driver_id != vk::DriverIdKHR::eMesaTurnip;
 #endif
     }
 
